{"id":"word:hebrew:H6083","type":"word","title":"עָפָר","subtitle":"H6083 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"dust (as powdered or gray); hence, clay , earth , mud","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עָפָר (H6083) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 110 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עָפָר (ʻâphâr) means dust (as powdered or gray); hence, clay , earth , mud First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 16 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עָפָר","transliteration":"ʻâphâr","pronunciation":"aw-fawr'","strong":"H6083","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6083","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["עָפָ֥ר","עֲפַ֣ר","עָפָ֖ר","עָפָֽר","עָפָ֣ר"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",38],["HRd/Ncmsa",18],["HNcmsc",10],["HR/Ncmsa",9],["HTd/Ncmsa",8],["HR/Ncmsc",5],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",3],["HNcmsc/Sp3fs",3],["HC/Ncmsa",3],["HC/R/Ncmsa",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"dust (as powdered or gray); hence, clay , earth , mud","usage":"ashes, dust, earth, ground, morter, powder, rubbish.","full":"H6083. aphar עָפָר noun masculine Lev 14:42 dry earth, dust ; — absolute ׳ע Gen 2:7 +, construct עֲפַר 13:16 +; suffix עֲפָרֵךְ Ezek 26:12 , עֲפָרוֺ Deut 9:21 , etc.; plural construct עַפְרֹת Job 28:6 ; Prov 8:26 ; &#8212; 1 literally: a. dry, loose earth , thrown (in malice) 2Sam 16:13 (|| אֲבָנִים ); ע ׳וַיַעֲלוּ עַלרֿאֹשׁ Josh 7:6 (J E; sign of grief), so Ezek 27:30 ; Lam 2:10 , and (with זָרַק ) Job 2:12 ; loose earth (on surface of ground) 1Kin 18:38 ; Amos 2:7 ; Micah 1:10 ; Isa 34:7 , 9 ; Lev 17:13 (H) Ezek 24:7 (in figurative), Num 5:17 ; Job 14:19 ; 38:38 ; 39:14 ; Gen 26:15 (R), made into siege works Hab 1:10 ; of sand-storm Deut 28:24 (+ אָבָק ); as serpent's food, token of punishment and humiliation, Gen 3:14 (J) Isa 65:25 (compare Micah 7:17 2e below); ע ׳זֹחֲלֵי Deut 32:24 (poem; compare 2e ). b. specifically as material of human body Gen 2:7 ; 3:19 (J), Eccl 3:20 , compare Job 4:19 ; 8:19 ; Psa 103:14 , to which it returns ( אֶלֿ שׁוּב ) Gen 3:19 ; Job 10:9 ; Psa 104:29 ; Eccl 3:20 ; so (with עַל ) Job 34:15 ; Eccl 12:7 . c. = surface of ground Exod 8:12 ; 8:13 (twice in verse); (P; ׳ע הָאָרַץ ), Job 19:25 ; Isa 25:12 ; 26:5 (both || אֶרֶץ ), surface of (whole) earth Job 41:25 , ע ׳מְחִלוֺת Isa 2:19 (for hiding), so ׳ע alone 2:10 , compare ע ׳חֹרֵי Job 30:6 ; = soil , 5:6 ; 14:8 . d. powder of anything pulverized Deut 9:21 (twice in verse) (compare דָּ֑ק || Exod 32:20 ), 2Kin 23:6 (twice in verse); 23:12 , 15 , so in simile 2Sam 22:43 = Psa 18:43 , hence = ashes 18:4 ; Num 19:17 . e. debris , of ruined city 1Kin 20:10 ; Ezek 26:4 , 12 ; Nehemiah 3:34; Neh 4:4 ; Psa 102:15 . The following are late: f. earth of the grave: ׳לֶע אֶשְׁכַּב Job 7:21 , so (with עַל ) 20:11 ; 21:26 , compare 17:16 ; ע ׳יוֺרְדֵי Psa 22:30 , ע ׳שֹׁכְנֵי Isa 26:19 , אַדְמַתעֿ ׳יְשֵׁנֵי Dan 12:2 ; עֲפַרמָֿוֶת Psa 22:16 ; ׳ע in figure 30:10 . g. mortar (i.e. dried mud) for plastering houses Lev 14:41-42 , 45 (P). h. (iron-) ore Job 28:2 ; זָהָב עַפְרֹת 28:6 gold-dust (but see סַמִּיר ). i. material of earth Isa 40:12 , compare תֵּבֵל עַפְרֹת ראֹשׁ Prov 8:26 the first of the earth particles of the world. 2 figurative: a. of abundance Gen 13:16 (twice in verse); 28:14 (all J) 2Chr 1:9 ; Job 27:16 ; Psa 78:27 (|| יַמִּים חוֺל ), compare יַעֲקֹב עֲפַר Num 23:10 (JE); with added idea of commonness, worthlessness Zeph 1:7 ; Zech 9:3 . b. of worthlessness (alone) Job 22:24 . c. simile of the scattered, dispersed 2Kin 13:7 ; ׳כֶּע Isa 41:2 (so van d. H. Ginsb; Baer ׳כֵּע ; on meaning see Du Che, reading תְּשִׂימֵם for יִתֵּן ). d. of self-abasement Gen 18:27 (+ אֵפַר ), וָאֵפֶר עַלעֿ ׳וְנִחַמְתִּי Job 42:6 , בֶּע ׳יִתֵּן מִּיהוּ Lam 3:29 . e. of humiliation (sitting or lying in dust) Isa 47:1 ; compare 29:4 (twice in verse), Job 16:15 ; 40:13 ; Psa 7:6 ; 44:26 ; 119:25 , simile Job 30:19 ; licking dust Psa 72:9 ; Isa 49:23 ; Micah 7:17 , compare Tel Amarna tikalu ipra (of enemies, see Wkl Altor. Forsch. iii. 291 ; also of serpent 1a above); of ׳י raising from the dust 1Sam 2:8 = Psa 113:7 , 1Kin 16:2 ; of lifting oneself Isa 52:2 .","rootNote":"from 6080 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 16 2","keyReferences":["1Kgs 16 2","1Kgs 18 38","1Kgs 20 10","1Sam 2 8","2Chr 1 9","2Kgs 13 7","2Kgs 23 4","2Kgs 23 6"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":110,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 16 2","book":"1Kgs","chapter":16,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֶ֣/עָפָ֔ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 18 38","book":"1Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":38,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֶ/עָפָ֑ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 10","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עֲפַ֣ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Sam 2 8","book":"1Sam","chapter":2,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מֵ/עָפָ֜ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 1 9","book":"2Chr","chapter":1,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כַּ/עֲפַ֥ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsc"},{"reference":"2Kgs 13 7","book":"2Kgs","chapter":13,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כֶּֽ/עָפָ֖ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 4","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עֲפָרָ֖/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 6","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/עָפָ֑ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 6","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עֲפָרָ֔/הּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3fs"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 12","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"עֲפָרָ֖/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 23 15","book":"2Kgs","chapter":23,"verse":1